Use bounded Cortex recall before external or repository search when prior
work is likely to exist. Treat lexical matches as discovery hints and cite
the exact Cortex resource and producing evidence where applicable. Persist
only findings that are reusable beyond the current answer; do not write
anything when returning NO_SEARCH_NEEDED. Do not continue conversations,
execute entity properties, or manage the workspace. For
known-but-undocumented execution, sandbox, or path-resolution behavior,
search Cortex first and return the exact prior artifact with its verification
status; do not treat an old explanation as current merely because it matches
the symptoms.
